  "cards": [
    {"dot":"cyan","title":"Pipeline state and recovery","items":["Site approval is written in an atomic transaction; the site pipeline task is enqueued on commit.","The worker advances each kept active Link from its persisted pipeline_stage; per-link exceptions set last_error and failed task state and emit a notification.","The custom db_worker command requeues interrupted running task results and unfinished pipeline work at startup; scheduled replays are enqueued by run_scheduled_replays."]},
    {"dot":"emerald","title":"What is persisted where","items":["The DB stores domain records and django-tasks-db queue/results. Trace bodies go through Django storage; the Trace row stores the key, backend, size and SHA-256.","Extracted rows, columns, classifications and normalized PlanRecord values are relational records. Publishing is a separate ops action that sends approved plan records to the catalog layer.","Redis is configured as Django's default cache; code uses it for OTP code/lockout state and DRF throttles. The task queue does not use Redis."]},
    {"dot":"rose","title":"Configuration-dependent details","items":["settings.py defaults to SQLite, while docker-compose.yaml sets DB_ENGINE=postgresql and provides PostgreSQL.","ARTIFACT_STORAGE_BACKEND defaults to the filesystem alias (value 'file'); selecting 's3' switches Django storage to S3Storage.","The LLM is called only when its configured OPENAI_BASE_URL is non-empty; discovery uses crawl4ai's statistical strategy without an LLM."]}
  ]
